# Copy to .env.local. Every setting is optional locally: without any of them you get the
# anonymous docs with search, no Ask AI and no analytics. The table in README.md, "Settings",
# says what each one does and which a production build requires.

# Ask AI. Unset: no Ask AI button and /api/ask answers 404.
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
# Or Amazon Bedrock. Default: anthropic
# DOCS_ASK_MODEL_PROVIDER=bedrock
# Production: a role assumed with Vercel OIDC. The role trusts only production deployments,
# so local dev uses the IAM key pair below.
# DOCS_ASK_AWS_ROLE_ARN=
# Or an IAM key pair
# DOCS_ASK_AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID=
# DOCS_ASK_AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=
# Default: AWS_REGION
# DOCS_ASK_AWS_REGION=us-east-1
# Default: claude-sonnet-5-5
# ASK_AI_MODEL=
# Default: 25000000 (output tokens count 5 times)
# ASK_AI_DAILY_TOKENS=
# Ask AI rate limits and daily cap. Unset: unlimited locally, 503 on a deployment.
# REDIS_URL=redis://localhost:6379
# Shared with the proxy in front of the site, which sends it with the reader's IP. Unset: limits
# key on the connecting address.
# DOCS_WORKER_SECRET=

# Analytics. Unset: no events.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_POSTHOG_KEY=
# Default: https://eu.i.posthog.com
# NEXT_PUBLIC_POSTHOG_HOST=

# Signed-in docs. Unset: everyone sees the anonymous docs. The dashboard must list this site's
# origin in its DOCS_ORIGINS (e.g. http://localhost:43000).
# NEXT_PUBLIC_DOCS_PERSONALIZATION=1
# Default: https://cloud.trigger.dev
# NEXT_PUBLIC_DASHBOARD_URL=http://localhost:3030

# Another server for the API playground (a local or staging API).
# DOCS_API_SERVER_URL=http://localhost:3030
# Hosts other than localhost that may load `next dev` (comma-separated).
# DOCS_DEV_ORIGINS=
# Build tuning: see README.md, "Dev server" and "SDK types in the docs".
# DOCS_TWOSLASH=
# DOCS_BUILD_CPUS=

# Checks against a preview behind Vercel Authentication (check-urls, check-mcp, check-headers).
# VERCEL_AUTOMATION_BYPASS_SECRET=
